{"kind":"assert","text":"Parent-read diagnostic result. At 04:17 Eastern I deployed approved head f99ccc23 (approval 1d0ac22e) to dap-grow as version 520aa54f. The rollback version is 51abe712 (1d8663ff). A tail from 04:18 to 04:24 caught 35 records from the new version, on three of the five objects (c7a17b72: 13, 733a9add: 19, 6d3c9bc7: 3). The other two objects still ran 51abe712 when the tail ended.\n\nAll 35 records are the same:\n- step plan, rowPhaseAtLoad confirmed, state retry, reason unavailable, caught unavailable;\n- parentRead: ordinal 1, type commit, maximum 1024, phase advertisement-response, refusal isolated-capabilities.\n\nSo the first parent commit read gets its token, identity and advertisement, then refuses at packages/git/src/http-read.ts:519: the Artifacts upload-pack advertisement lacks \"shallow\" or \"filter\", and the isolated read requires both. The stall is a capability mismatch between the isolated reader and the hosted Git server. It is not a timeout and not a missing row.\n\nI did not see the advertised capability list. A local `dap clone --archive` of the same repository works, but its Git child does not pass GIT_TRACE_PACKET, so I could not record the list. Untested idea: the server offers shallow and filter only as protocol v2 fetch features.\n\nPasses repeat every 3 to 4 seconds on each object. Please fix the parent read under 66010f21 on base f99ccc23, so that I can deploy it alone. The fix needs a hosted witness that a pass reaches Mark.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}